One block per key in config.yaml. Every job a key controls is listed together, 
because a key is a single choice: a model that wins one of its jobs and loses  
another is not an upgrade. UNKNOWN means the incumbent has never been measured 
on its own job -- run the command shown and it resolves.                       

Model identifiers are endpoint-specific: minimax/minimax-m3 (OpenRouter) and   
minimax-m3:cloud (Ollama cloud) are different serving stacks and are NOT       
treated as the same measurement. If a similar name appears in a table below but
the incumbent still reads UNKNOWN, that is deliberate -- benchmark the         
identifier you actually route to.                                              

